On Tue, 9 Jan 2007, azgor wrote:
>
> [2]: Is it possible to bury a wand of digging? If so, it should refuse
> to allow itself to be buried, unless it has been cancelled. This should
> break the boulder instead of filling the pit. --BenUrban

   Breaking the boulder is a little strong. Perhaps --- I don't really
know how rotting works, but --- a buried wand of digging would have
a timer like a rotting organic item, and when its timer was up, or
at some random time, it would pop to the surface. "You see a wand
emerge from the ground!" (Or, to avoid needing an appropriate message,
have the wand only appear when it's out of sight of the player. But
that's less elegant, because the player can't camp next to a buried
wand to observe its behavior in its natural habitat. :)

