> [21]: <Tropsy> I always thought wearing a fedora should make you always
> dodge rolling boulder traps, but then make the fedora fall on the
> ground --Yui

   Yet another old idea. I don't see why you should drop your hat; that's
just annoying to the player. Gratuitous annoyance is a bad idea; let's
just pretend that the character dropped his hat, and then once the
boulder was past, he went back and picked it up. No need to force the
player to simulate those actions.
   ...Unless you were thinking of a rolling boulder trap as a way to
remove a cursed fedora? That's interesting, but not useful enough to
be worth the annoyance in non-cursed cases.

